<h1>shortest common supersequence</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Find the shortest string that contains two or more <a href="string.html"><em>strings</em></a> as <a href="subsequence.html"><em>subsequences</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="shortestCommonSuperstring.html"><em>shortest common superstring</em></a>, <a href="longestCommonSubsequence.html"><em>longest common subsequence</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

